  "changes": {
    "region_copy": "Worker finds one moved rectangle per capture and sends COPY=10. A per-pixel model of what the viewer holds decides which tiles the copy makes exact, so a wrong guess costs a repaint and late strips at an edge cannot stop the interior.",
    "video_freeze": "After the first copy of an epoch, video keeps the last encoded value under tiles the viewer holds exactly, so moved pixels do not also consume bitrate.",
    "strips": "Exposed strips and pixels returning from video need no settling or video fence. An isolated strip may wait 400 ms; under sustained copies it hands over to video after 120 ms, for 150 ms renewed by further changes.",
    "input_response": "The first change per tile after a pointer press, release or wheel event, when at most 32 tiles changed, takes the same immediate path.",
    "qp_floor_and_vbr": "Cropped NVENC, QSV and VA-API use a QP floor of 20 and no CBR.",
    "exact_flight_control": "Exact bytes in flight are limited by viewer acknowledgement delay (8-256 KiB), and path-limited delivery rate is given to the worker, because the video target does not describe a path while video is idle.",
    "minimum_crop": "Crops are at least 192x128: AMD VA-API refuses below 128 pixels and the failure stopped video."
  },
