  "findings": [
    "NVENC with qmin 0 spent 100-150 KB/s on a static crop at about 1.7 KB per picture; with a floor of 20 the same pictures cost about 50 bytes. It also removes bursts of 20-50 KB pictures for invisible detail, which had pushed the source below 50 fps at 8 Mbit/s.",
    "The clip fps drop in exp192 was caused by enabling copies, shown by clean copy-disabled controls, but through encoder rate control on a different crop rather than through copy commands.",
    "Removing CBR removed the native source-age failure: about 580 ms excess on QSV and VA-API became about 200-300 ms. The open question about the native 400 ms limit no longer blocks.",
    "Once video idles, the estimator gets no signal that a path narrowed, so exact traffic alone could fill a 2 Mbit/s path and queue for seconds. Acknowledgement delay detects that independently of video.",
    "aiortc SCTP starts at 3.6 KB and grows only while fully used, limiting sparse exact bursts to about one window per round trip."
  ],
  "corrections": [
    "Earlier QSM responsiveness runs had the fixture page and a playing clip behind the bench window while RDP had neither; their figures are withdrawn. See docs/rdp-ui-responsiveness-20261104.json.",
    "Control runs and one bench round overlapped on one guest after a chain script was stopped without its running child; those runs were discarded and lanes now hold a lock.",
    "A version-number replacement in a generated script changed the PVE address, and scp tried 194.168.64.20 twice. TCP port 22 timed out, so nothing was transferred. Replacement now skips addresses and the chain refuses generated files with a wrong address."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Launch/ACL mocked; dedicated guests only. Firefox on Linux only: candidate behaviour on Chrome/macOS is unverified because the Mac stayed unreachable.",
    "The bench backdrop is flat, a best case for exposed strips; text behind a moving window is covered by worker oracle tests, not by a live run.",
    "One motion vector per capture. Fractional or animated scrolling stays on video and was not measured.",
    "QP floor is not qualified on HEVC, and VM+LXC encoder matrix, long sessions and A/V remain open.",
    "Exact UI stays off by default; these results apply only with it enabled.",
    "Small run counts; the 400 ms excess limit is within spread of the PVE runs."
  ],
  "remaining": [
    "Chrome and macOS verification when the Mac returns",
    "Text behind a moving window live",
    "HEVC and full VM+LXC encoder matrix",
    "Typing and first-response gap of about 20 ms",
    "Opus DTX for idle bytes",
    "TCP-repair recut, long sessions, A/V",
    "All packages, signed checksums/APT, docs, qualified rollout"
  ]
}
